WEBVTT

1

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.750

Attention!



2

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:25.540

I will now explain to you the details

of the Trost Recovery Operation!



3

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.500

Let me start by introducing this fellow!



4

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.330

This is Eren Jaeger,

a member of the Cadets!



5

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.000

He is the successful result



6

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.700

of our top-secret Titan

transformation experiments!



7

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.620

In Titan form, he will lift that

giant rock near the front gate,



8

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.790

carry it to the wrecked gate,



9

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:48.830

and seal the hole!



10

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.000

As for <i>you</i>,



11

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.700

you're to defend him from the

other Titans while he carries the rock!



12

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.500

Should this operation succeed,



13

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:05.500

humanity will have taken back land

from the Titans for the very first time!



14

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.370

Indeed, it may

seem extraordinarily small



15

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:14.410

when compared to what

humanity has given up this far!



16

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:16.000

However...!



17

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.750

For humankind,

that single, small step...



18

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.830

...will be a great leap forward!



19

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.620

Eren! Don't you recognize me?!



20

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.450

I'm Mikasa!



21

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.910

Part of your family!



22

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:44.830

Dodge, Ackermann!



23

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:49.750

What the hell?!



24

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.750

He's just a regular, dumb Titan!



25

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.330

Change of plans!



26

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:58.200

We're to defend Jaeger from the

other Titans until we can recover him!



27

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.160

He holds a precious chance for humanity.



28

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.700

We can't abandon him just like that!



29

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.950

Where am I?



30

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.120

I'm home...



31

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.370

Jean!



32

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.910

Why isn't he using his ODM gear?!



33

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.040

Oh no!



34

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.250

Don't tell me it's malfunctioning?!



35

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.830

I'll manage somehow!



36

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.410

Mikasa!



37

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:27.790

What happened to the plan?!



38

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:29.200

It's failed!



39

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.660

We're fighting because

we can't leave Eren behind!



40

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.000

But there are too many Titans...



41

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.410

At this rate, we'll be wiped out!



42

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.830

From the back of the head

to the nape of the neck...



43

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:46.750

...1 meter high and

10 centimeters across!



44

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.790

Eren... Answer me...



45

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:57.080

Even though just one step outside

the wall lies a hellish world...



46

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:02.410

Why did you want to

venture into the outside world?!



47

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.660

Why?



48

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.500

Because...



49

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.950

...I was born in this world!



50

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.000

Eren!



51

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:44.700

<i>Unknown are the names</i>

<i>of the flowers that have been trampled</i>



52

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:50.160

<i>Birds have fallen to the earth</i>

<i>and long for the wind</i>



53

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:55.250

<i>Prayers won't solve anything</i>



54

00:03:55.250 --> 00:04:00.580

<i>Only the will to fight</i>

<i>can change the here and now!</i>



55

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:05.910

<i>O pigs who laugh at the resolve</i>

<i>to walk over corpses to move forward</i>



56

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.450

<i>Livestock complacency? False prosperity?</i>



57

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:11.330

<i>Give us the freedom of dying,</i>

<i>starving wolves!</i>



58

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:16.700

<i>The humiliation of being caged</i>

<i>is what triggers us to fight back</i>



59

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:22.000

<i>We hunters slaughter prey</i>

<i>beyond the castle walls,</i>



60

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.200

<i>consumed with surging bloodlust,</i>



61

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:34.120

<i>as our crimson bows and arrows</i>

<i>pierce scarlet holes into the twilight</i>



62

00:04:56.450 --> 00:05:01.330

"Primal Desire"

"The Struggle for Trost, Part 9"



63

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:13.660

Damn... I can't believe <i>I'm</i>

draggin' everyone down...



64

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.620

Will this really work out somehow?



65

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.830

We can't go on, Captain!



66

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:41.250

It's just us now!



67

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:44.950

Let's fall back to the rock for now!



68

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:51.870

Situation report!



69

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.620

Five Titans coming from the gate!



70

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.870

There's no way I can just sit

around and wait until the coast is clear!



71

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:11.330

Jean!



72

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.950

So his gear <i>is </i>busted!



73

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.580

What's going on?!



74

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:18.750

Crap!



75

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.250

What the hell?!



76

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:23.330

Damn it! Of all the times...!



77

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:27.700

Jean! Stay calm!



78

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.160

Marco!



79

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.000

What are you doing?!



80

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:46.500

Man!



81

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.410

Don't go causin' trouble for us!



82

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.120

Damn! Why is the trigger so stiff?!



83

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.120

Jean!



84

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:13.290

Oww!



85

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.790

What are you doing?!



86

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.540

Same to you! Now get outta there!



87

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.500

You guys are damn reckless!



88

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.040

No, <i>you </i>are!



89

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:56.080

That scared the hell out of me!



90

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.410

Look!



91

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.500

Eren...



92

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.910

Mikasa!



93

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.120

Armin!



94

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.950

Eren prevailed!



95

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:45.500

He's trying to fulfill

his responsibility now!



96

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.870

Now if we just cover

him until he reaches the gate...



97

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:51.250

...victory will be ours!



98

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:57.410

Defend him!



99

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.660

Even if it costs us our lives...



100

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:03.120

...we <i>must </i>let Eren reach the gate!



101

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.870

Do <i>not </i>let the Titans get near him!



102

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:10.540

We gotta give Eren backup! Keep 'em off him!



103

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:16.160

You two head to Eren!



104

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:19.040

That's an order! Is that clear?!



105

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:20.450

Yes, Sir!



106

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.540

The Mitabi team!



107

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.250

What are you doing?!



108

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.580

The Titans are ignoring us now!



109

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:33.040

Our only choice is to get close

enough to grab their attention!



110

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:35.000

Look this way, damn it!



111

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:40.120

Or else we'll shove our blades

up your smelly asses and kill you!



112

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.580

--Here they come!

--We got two of 'em!



113

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:48.660

Run! Run for the buildings!



114

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:50.040

That's insane!



115

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.660

Setting foot down there is suicide!



116

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:56.040

And they have no way to

fight without horses or buildings!



117

00:09:56.040 --> 00:10:01.040

No... That's the only option now.



118

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.290

Follow Mitabi Team!



119

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:08.750

Armin. We need to go, too.



120

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:12.370

This way!



121

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:14.330

Come get me!



122

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.950

My body feels...



123

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:27.080

...like it's about to be crushed into a pulp...



124

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:32.000

Mikasa... Armin...



125

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.450

What are you doing?



126

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:37.870

You'll end up Titan food if

you walk around down there...!



127

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:41.040

C'mon! Hurry this way, you slowpoke!



128

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.450

Come get me!



129

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.540

H-Hey!



130

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.500

Mitabi!



131

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:57.000

Why did you want



132

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:59.870

to venture into

the outside world?



133

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:07.910

From the moment

we're born, we're all...



134

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:09.330

...free...



135

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:17.700

Some might try to deny that,

but it doesn't matter how strong they are!



136

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:24.450

Fiery waters... Lands of ice...

Or whatever else!



137

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.910

Whoever gets to see those things



138

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:31.000

will have the greatest

freedom this world has to offer!



139

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:34.660

Fight!



140

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:37.410

If anything is worth

giving your life, it's that!



141

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:43.830

It doesn't matter how

terrifying the world may be!



142

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:50.830

It doesn't matter

how cruel the world may be!



143

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:53.040

Fight!



144

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:55.080

Fight!



145

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.200

Fight!



146

00:11:57.830 --> 00:11:59.250

Fight!



147

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:04.750

There's still a Titan ahead!



148

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.370

I'll handle this!



149

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:13.540

Out of the way!



150

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:38.750

Go, Eren!



151

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:41.160

Fight!



152

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:08.580

Everyone...



153

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:12.080

Your deaths <i>weren't </i>in vain...



154

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:21.410

Today, for the first time in history...



155

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:24.290

...humanity has beaten the Titans!



156

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:26.540

Yellow smoke shell spotted!



157

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:30.040

It seems the operation...

was a success!



158

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.910

Send in additional reinforcements!



159

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:36.660

Rescue the Elite Squad!



160

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.870

The remaining Titans are coming!



161

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.660

Head up the wall!



162

00:13:57.660 --> 00:14:00.160

I'll withdraw after I've recovered Eren!



163

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:04.160

Armin! How's Eren?!



164

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:07.080

He's unbelievably hot to the touch!



165

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:10.870

We need to hurry...

and get him up the wall...!



166

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:16.620

Part of his body is fused to it!



167

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.540

--I can't pull him free!

--Then we'll have to cut!



168

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.950

W-Wait! Please!



169

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.160

Eren! Armin!



170

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:57.700

Mikasa...



171

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:58.910

Huh?!



172

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:00.410

Those are...



173

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:05.370

The wings...



174

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:07.200

...of freedom...



175

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:16.200

Hey. You kids.



176

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:19.290

What exactly is going on here?



177

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.410

Afterward, thanks to the actions



178

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:31.950

of the Scout Regiment and the

Garrison Regiment's Corps of Engineers,



179

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:36.250

Wall Rose once

again held the Titans at bay.



180

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:45.160

Taking out the rest of the Titans

trapped inside Trost took a full day,



181

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:49.370

during which the wall-mounted

cannons fired nonstop.



182

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:53.870

Most of the Titans that

had gathered by the wall



183

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:56.200

were wiped out by explosive shells.



184

00:15:56.200 --> 00:16:02.000

The few that remained were

mostly mopped up by the Scouts.



185

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:08.830

During this, one 4-meter

Titan and one 7-meter Titan



186

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:12.410

were successfully captured alive.



187

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:14.370

However...



188

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:18.000

207 people were dead or missing,



189

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:21.200

and 897 were injured.



190

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:25.580

Although this was the first time

humanity had stopped a Titan invasion,



191

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:32.080

far too many people had been lost

to celebrate this historic achievement.



192

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:53.950

Hey...



193

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:01.870

Are you...



194

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.950

...Marco?



195

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:10.290

Do you know his name, cadet?



196

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:11.910

I <i>wondered </i>where he was...



197

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:17.080

But... he's the last person who would ever...



198

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:19.040

Marco...



199

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:20.620

What happened?



200

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:26.910

D-Did someone--anyone--see

how he went out?



201

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:28.620

What is his name?



202

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:31.410

Tell me if you know. Quickly.



203

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:36.830

Do you understand, cadet?



204

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:40.120

Two days have passed since

we sealed the hole with the rock.



205

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.830

Yet we <i>still </i>haven't

rounded up all the bodies.



206

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:47.750

At this rate,

an epidemic could break out.



207

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.910

We <i>must </i>prevent a secondary disaster.



208

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:54.330

There's no time to lament our

comrades' deaths yet.



209

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:55.950

Understand?



210

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:06.160

Member of the 104th Cadet Corps

and Captain of Squad 19...



211

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:08.830

...Marco Bodt.



212

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.160

Marco.



213

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.660

I'm glad you knew his name.



214

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:14.620

Let's continue.



215

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:27.250

What <i>is </i>this...?



216

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:31.830

Leftover Titan vomit.



217

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:34.080

Apparently they don't

have digestive systems,



218

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:38.450

so they puke people out like

that once they've had their fill.



219

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.500

You can't be serious...



220

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:45.080

Damn... There's no way of

telling who's who in there!



221

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:50.250

I'm sorry...



222

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:56.160

I'm sorry...



223

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.540

It's no use apologizing.



224

00:18:58.540 --> 00:19:00.750

We need to hurry and give them a funeral.



225

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:28.450

Have any questions?



226

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:34.870

Commander Erwin, the head of

the Scouts Regiment's Task Force...



227

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:38.040

...and Captain Levi!



228

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:40.370

U-Umm...



229

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:46.000

Where... am I?



230

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:55.290

It should be obvious.

Let's just say it's a dungeon.



231

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:59.120

You're currently in the

custody of the Military Police.



232

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:03.580

Only just now were

we permitted to see you.



233

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:07.450

That key...!



234

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:10.120

Yes. It's yours.



235

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:12.040

I'll return it later.



236

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:17.160

Dr. Jaeger's basement,

in your home in Shiganshina...



237

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:20.910

A secret surrounding

the Titans is there, correct?



238

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:23.290

Yes. I think so.



239

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:25.700

That's what my father said.



240

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:30.000

And you've lost your memory,

<i>and </i>your old man's gone missing...



241

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.870

Pretty convenient story, if you ask me.



242

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.450

Levi.



243

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:38.580

We've already concluded he

has no reason to lie. You know that.



244

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:40.790

There is still so little we know,



245

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:45.290

but for now, I feel the most important

thing is to ask about your intentions.



246

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:48.080

My intentions?



247

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:51.370

If we want to check out your home,



248

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:55.540

we'll need to take back

Shiganshina District along Wall Maria.



249

00:20:56.500 --> 00:21:01.950

Sealing the damaged gate there would

be the best way to accomplish that.



250

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:04.790

Which means we'll need your Titan ability.



251

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:10.410

Naturally, it's a Titan

that will determine our fate.



252

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:13.870

The Colossal Titan

and the Armored Titan



253

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.660

most likely work the same way as you.



254

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:20.910

Your intentions are the key.



255

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:25.160

The key to saving humankind from this despair.



256

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:29.410

I'm...



257

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:35.950

I'm going to drive out...



258

00:21:35.950 --> 00:21:40.540

...every last one from this world!



259

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:44.040

Hey. Answer the damn question, you twit.



260

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:46.660

What do you want to do?



261

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:53.660

I want to join the Scouts...



262

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:57.040

...and slaughter every Titan I can!



263

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:01.580

Ah. Not bad.



264

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:09.870

Erwin. I'll take responsibility for him.



265

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:12.410

Let the higher-ups know.



266

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:15.580

I don't necessarily trust him, though.



267

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:18.000

If he betrays us or goes out of control,



268

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.700

I'll kill him on the spot.



269

00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:22.870

The top brass won't complain.



270

00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:26.000

Because I'm the only one cut out for this.



271

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:28.080

You're in.



272

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:31.410

I'll make you a member of the Scouts.



273

00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:57.870

<i>Your dreams are where your heart is</i>



274

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:04.120

<i>They're more fragile than life itself</i>



275

00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:08.790

<i>Over and over you cast them aside,</i>

<i>only to find more</i>



276

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:15.450

<i>Now, rest in peace</i>



277

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:26.790

<i>Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for</i>



278

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:37.080

<i>and the more we forget</i>

<i>the more we remember again</i>



279

00:23:37.080 --> 00:23:43.040

<i>In this beautiful, cruel world</i>



280

00:23:43.040 --> 00:23:48.200

<i>all I can do is ask why we're still alive</i>



281

00:23:48.200 --> 00:23:53.910

<i>Oh, with our strength--and our weakness--</i>



282

00:23:53.910 --> 00:23:59.580

<i>what are we going to protect if there's no sense</i>



283

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:03.000

<i>to anything anymore?</i>



284

00:24:09.830 --> 00:24:12.290

A special court-martial.



285

00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:15.080

After being held in an underground cell,



286

00:24:15.080 --> 00:24:18.750

Eren is dragged into a courthouse

filled with the heads of each regiment.



287

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:21.830

What happens there will

determine whether he lives or dies.



288

00:24:21.830 --> 00:24:23.370

"Can't Look into His Eyes Yet

Eve of the Counterattack, Part 1"

